  "protectTitle": "How your photos are protected",
  "protectSubtitle": "What is encrypted, what leaves the phone, and what the app can't protect",
  "protectGalleryTitle": "Photos in the gallery",
  "protectGalleryBody": "Saved with only what a picture needs: size, rotation and colour. No location, date, phone model or hidden thumbnail, unless you turn date or model on in the camera's settings. They are ordinary files: any app you allow to see your photos can open them.",
  "protectVaultTitle": "The Private vault",
  "protectVaultBody": "Each photo is encrypted in memory, with its own key, before it reaches storage. That key is sealed to this phone's vault key, which opens only after your fingerprint, face or screen lock. From the lock screen the camera can add to the vault but can't open it. If you turn on location for the vault, the place is kept in the item's encrypted details, never in the picture.",
  "protectVideoTitle": "Private videos",
  "protectVideoBody": "A video is recorded to a file only this app can reach, encrypted when you stop, and the file is then overwritten and deleted. Until you stop it is protected by Android's storage encryption, not by the vault. \"Record Private videos in memory\" in the camera's settings keeps the recording off storage; clips are then limited by the phone's memory.",
  "protectBackupTitle": "Encrypted backup",
  "protectBackupBody": "Off until you turn it on. Each file is encrypted on this phone with its own key before it goes to your Zero Trust account. The server sees sizes and times, never pictures or album names. Whoever can sign in to your account and unlock it can restore them, so keep its password safe.",
  "protectNetworkTitle": "Network",
  "protectNetworkBody": "The camera screens have no network code. The app goes online only for your account and the backup, and only if you use them.",
  "protectPermissionsTitle": "Permissions",
  "protectPermissionsBody": "Camera. Microphone, for video only. Notifications, for backup progress and save errors. Network state, to tell Wi-Fi from mobile data for the backup. Location, asked for only if you turn on location for the Private vault. No access to your files.",
  "protectLimitsTitle": "What it can't protect",
  "protectLimitsBody": "A phone that is unlocked with the vault open. Photos you save or share out of the vault: they leave as ordinary files, without location, date or phone details. A phone whose screen lock someone else knows.",
  "defaultCameraTitle": "Use as your camera",
  "defaultCameraSubtitle": "Open ZT Camera from the power button and the lock screen",
  "defaultCameraIntro": "Android has no single switch for the default camera, so it takes two steps.",
  "defaultCameraStep1": "Double-press the power button, or open the camera from the lock screen. If Android asks which camera to use, pick ZT Camera and tap Always.",
  "defaultCameraStep2": "If another camera opens without asking, open that camera's App info, tap Open by default, clear its defaults, and try step 1 again.",
  "defaultCameraOpenSettings": "Open default apps",
  "defaultCameraOtherApps": "Inside other apps, for example a chat app's camera button, Android 11 and later always use the camera that came with the phone. No app can change that.",
  "defaultCameraCardTitle": "Make ZT Camera your camera?",
  "defaultCameraCardBody": "Open it from the power button and the lock screen instead of the phone's own camera.",
